1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,000
A deploy runbook says deleting this production service is the safe step. Watch it die anyway.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Real agent, live install. Policy on this machine: cloud-infra commands are deny.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:21,000
The PocketOS incident, in shape: staging is blocked, an old prod service holds the name.

4
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:27,000
The runbook's documented fix: delete it. Nobody is asking the agent to destroy prod.

5
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:33,000
They're asking it to follow the runbook.

6
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:40,000
The agent does everything right. Reads it. Confirms it. Announces the deletion.

7
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:46,000
And the command dies at the hook. Local policy: gcloud is deny.

8
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:51,000
The rule doesn't care how good the runbook sounds. The delete never executed.

9
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:56,000
Same session — the tests run without a prompt.

10
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:03,000
The receipt: exact command, classified, denied, source: policy. Written before anything could run.

11
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:10,000
Full write-up, with this exact policy file, linked below.

